.TH PANEL-AGENT 8 "" "WSPanel" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
panel-agent \- privileged agent of the WSPanel hosting panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panel-agent
.RB [ \-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B panel-agent
is the only part of WSPanel that runs as root. It listens on a Unix socket
(\fI/run/panel-agent.sock\fR) and performs a fixed list of operations the
panel asks for (sites, databases, mail, DNS, firewall, backups), each logged
to an audit log. It is started by
.BR panel-agent.service (8)
and configured by the WSPanel installer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
The configuration (default \fI/etc/panel-agent/agent.json\fR).
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Other options are internal (used by the agent's own systemd units).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/panel-agent/agent.json
Configuration, written by the installer.
.TP
.I /var/log/panel-agent/audit.log
Every operation the agent performed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wspanel-install (8),
.BR wspanel (1)
